{"availability":"available","full":"marcturu/glitch-void","name":"glitch-void","description":"Interactive retro terminal game built with Next.js, React, TypeScript and Tailwind CSS. Simulates a system progressively collapsing through dynamic log generation, binary rain, CRT scanlines, animated UI elements and a custom terminal cursor, combining component-based architecture with immersive visual effects.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-03T17:06:55Z","updated":"2026-10-08T09:27:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://glitch-void.vercel.app","topics":["git","nextjs","reactjs","software-development","tailwindcss","typescript","ui-design","vercel"],"demo":"https://glitch-void.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.654Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.654Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.654Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.654Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project consists of a Next.js-based web game. It implements a retro terminal that boots up, starts logging — and slowly falls apart. Errors creep in, the signal degrades, and after a few seconds the system collapses into the void, but there's a way to save it. Built with Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript 5.7, and Tailwind CSS 4 — featuring animated binary rain, CRT scanlines, a custom cursor, and a self-evolving terminal log simulation with a ticking clock."],"features":["Terminal Simulation: A living, breathing terminal interface (terminal-simulation.tsx) that autonomously generates and collapses log lines over time, mimicking a system spiralling into glitch entropy.","Custom Cursor: Blinking terminal-style cursor (cursor.tsx) for an authentic retro aesthetic.","Log Lines: Individually styled log entries (log-line.tsx) that appear and decay as the simulation progresses.","CRT Scanlines: Retro scanline overlay effect (scanlines.tsx) replicating the look of an old cathode-ray tube monitor.","Binary Rain: Animated binary background (binary-rain.tsx) rendered as a visual layer beneath the terminal."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marcturu/glitch-void/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a2cce1afbf506b0d8af5659b696aa3f4d745a5fe49e2b9c68cddc7afcf089c86","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.774Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.774Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project consists of a Next.js-based web game. It implements a retro terminal that boots up, starts logging — and slowly falls apart. Errors creep in, the signal degrades, and after a few seconds the system collapses into the void, but there's a way to save it. Built with Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript 5.7, and Tailwind CSS 4 — featuring animated binary rain, CRT scanlines, a custom cursor, and a self-evolving terminal log simulation with a ticking clock.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marcturu/glitch-void/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a2cce1afbf506b0d8af5659b696aa3f4d745a5fe49e2b9c68cddc7afcf089c86","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marcturu/glitch-void/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.775Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T09:27:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/marcturu/glitch-void/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T21:28:08.775Z","hash":"a2cce1afbf506b0d8af5659b696aa3f4d745a5fe49e2b9c68cddc7afcf089c86","originalBytes":3382,"storedBytes":3382,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["terminal","log","animated","bash","binary","cursor","gameplay","npm","simulation","crt","desktop","mobile","retro","screenshots","background","binary-rain.tsx","blinking","clone","collapses","css","cursor.tsx","custom","effect","entries","game","gameplay.png","install","layer","lines","log-line.tsx","next.js","overlay","project","rain","react","run","save","scanline","scanline